  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Description\n\nNo avatar can be set to be taller than 1.3m. The UI shows the full circle, but has a line and tick preventing you from using the rest of the circular input.\n\n  \n\nIf an avatar was already taller than this, it remained so until the player interacted with the height control. In that case it would change to 1.3m and from that point can not be made taller.\n\nIn the Avatar settings menu, under IKs, an extraneous colon appears in the menu, which appears to be related to the problem. Example: \"\"arm-length\" and \"height:\".\n\nReproduction Steps\n\nNo workaround. To reproduce, try to set any avatar to be taller than 1.3 meters via the radial menu in-game.\n\nDetails\n\n- Category: Avatar\n\n- Frequency: Always\n\n---\n\nplatform: PC (platform: Windows, store: Steam, headset: None)\n\nrawPlatform: WindowsPlayer\n\nclientVersion: 2026.4.1p1-1937-299983b13b-Release\n\nunityVersion: 6000.0.67f1-DWR\n\nIn-Client Report",
